// The node number of the function called text_name, adding it when it is new, and recording its file:line when text_location is not "" and its case count when number_cases is not negative. A callee read from an edge row has a location but no case count, a function row has both, a builtin has neither, so a node keeps whatever it was told at any point.
call_graph_intern(string[][] strings_graph, int[][] table_graph, string text_name, string text_location, int number_cases) {
  int number_old = len(strings_graph[(import call_graph_string_name)]);
  int number_identifier = graph_node(strings_graph[(import call_graph_string_node_key)], table_graph[(import call_graph_integer_node_value)], table_graph[(import call_graph_integer_node_used)], table_graph[(import call_graph_integer_node_count)], strings_graph[(import call_graph_string_name)], text_name);
  call_graph_slot(strings_graph, table_graph, number_identifier, number_old, text_location, number_cases);
} return int number_identifier;
